+## First-dungeon statuses (#359)
+
+Scope: the 26 first-dungeon moves of [`move-effects.md`](move-effects.md) (#357). No random traps on floors 1-3. Ability-caused statuses (Synchronize `0x19`, Static and similar) stay [lead]. Yawning and confusion are not in the list and stay open. Chain steps are in `TickStatusAndHealthRegen` `02185C70`. Static reads from the export (STAMP 2026-11-14). Duration pairs were read from RAM on floor 1 with `verification/v7-trace/` style py-desmume (probe `pools.py`, scratch only), which reads ranges and does not apply a status. **No status was applied or observed at runtime**, so every per-turn effect is a static read, and the duration tag below rests on the pair read plus the proven roll rule.
+
+**Roll rule** (#191 P1, re-read at `0219CF28` and `0219D014`/`0219D058`): `roll = min + DungeonRandInt(max - min)`, `max` exclusive. **If min == max it draws nothing.** `0219CF28` forces a minimum of 1; with flag != 0 and a monster it halves for IQ `0x12` and caps at 5 for ability `0x14`. Setters store `roll + 1`. This corrects the earlier "one `DungeonRandRange` per wrapper" claim for equal ranges (burn, flinch, yawn draw 0).
